{"id": "idaho-2", "headline": "Nampa council to hear water rate increase proposal", "source": "KIVI", "url": "https://www.kivitv.com/nampa/nampa-city-council-to-consider-water-irrigation-system-rate-hikes", "published": "2026-11-24", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["The Nampa City Council is considering higher residential water rates, with a public hearing set for Monday, December 21, at City Hall. The city says the increase is needed for maintenance and replacing aging pipes. The average monthly water bill would rise 8. 4%, or $1. 48, from $17. 68 to $19. 16, though some customers could see up to 13. 8% more depending on usage and lot size. Irrigation service would go up about $26. 02 a year for a typical 10,700 square foot lot. The city says 112 of its 646 miles of water pipe are at or near the end of their lifespan, and there were 63 mainline breaks in the past year. Source: KIVI."], "qr": {"n": 37, "rows": ["1111111011110100010000101100001111111", "1000001010010010110000101000101000001", "1011101001000111111011000111001011101", "1011101000011110011011110111001011101", "1011101010011110001001100110001011101", "1000001011101010000011000000101000001", "1111111010101010101010101010101111111", "0000000011000011001000101010000000000", "1110011011011011000010010011111110011", "1011110011001101100111011101101000111", "0000101011101101000100010101100101011", "1111000110111010101010101011101100011", "1100101100100000100010001000101001011", "0110110001000101000101010001101101111", "0110001111110111011110011011011110001", "1100100011000000101100001011111100000", "1111001001111000100100001000101001011", "0010010100001101101110111101001101111", "0111001011101111010100110111000010001", "1010110001011010100010100010011011000", "0010011111000001100110001001101100001", "0010000100100101110111011011101101011", "1111111100110011111111110101100100001", "1000100011000010101010110000010101000", "0001001110111001000100011001011000001", "0000010000001001110110011111101101011", "11110011